  "text": "We are given two quadratic equations:\n\n1. $ x^2 + bx + c = 0 $\n2. $ y^2 - cy + 4 = 0 $\n\nWe are told that they have **a common root**, and $ c > 0 $. We are also told that:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{8b}\n$$\n\nand we need to determine the **largest possible value** for $ c $ such that:\n\n- $ b > 0 $\n- $ c > 0 $\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Use the common root\n\nLet the common root be $ \\alpha $. Then:\n\n$$\n\\alpha^2 + b\\alpha + c = 0 \\quad \\text{(1)}\n$$\n$$\n\\alpha^2 - c\\alpha + 4 = 0 \\quad \\text{(2)}\n$$\n\nSubtracting (2) from (1):\n\n$$\n(\\alpha^2 + b\\alpha + c) - (\\alpha^2 - c\\alpha + 4) = 0\n\\Rightarrow (b\\alpha + c\\alpha) + (c - 4) = 0\n\\Rightarrow \\alpha(b + c) + (c - 4) = 0\n\\Rightarrow \\alpha(b + c) = 4 - c \\quad \\text{(3)}\n$$\n\nSolve for $ b $:\n\n$$\nb = \\frac{4 - c}{c} = \\frac{4}{c} - 1 \\quad \\text{(4)}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Use the given expression for $ c $\n\nWe are told:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{8b}\n$$\n\nSubstitute $ b = \\frac{4}{c} - 1 $ into this equation:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{8\\left( \\frac{4}{c} - 1 \\right)}\n$$\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{8 \\left( \\frac{4 - c}{c} \\right)} = \\frac{c^2 - 16}{\\frac{8(4 - c)}{c}} = \\frac{c(c^2 - 16)}{8(4 - c)}\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{c(c^2 - 16)}{8(4 - c)}\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by $ 8(4 - c) $:\n\n$$\n8c(4 - c) = c(c^2 - 16)\n$$\n\nDivide both sides by $ c $ (since $ c \\ne 0 $):\n\n$$\n8(4 - c) = c^2 - 16\n$$\n\n$$\n32 - 8c = c^2 - 16\n$$\n\nBring all terms to one side:\n\n$$\nc^2 + 8c - 48 = 0\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Solve the quadratic equation\n\n$$\nc^2 + 8c - 48 = 0\n$$\n\nUse the quadratic formula:\n\n$$\nc = \\frac{-8 \\pm \\sqrt{8^2 + 4 \\cdot 48}}{2} = \\frac{-8 \\pm \\sqrt{64 + 192}}{2} = \\frac{-8 \\pm \\sqrt{256}}{2} = \\frac{-8 \\pm 16}{2}\n$$\n\nSo:\n\n- $ c = \\frac{-8 + 16}{2} = 4 $\n- $ c = \\frac{-8 - 16}{2} = -12 $\n\nWe are told that $ c > 0 $, so we discard $ c = -12 $.\n\nThus, the only valid solution is:\n\n$$\nc = 4\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{4}\n$$",
